  "term": "diagnostic test",
  "definition": "A diagnostic test is a method used to detect whether a person likely has a particular condition by classifying cases as present or absent. Its performance is judged by how accurately it identifies true cases and non-cases, such as through sensitivity, specificity, and overall discrimination.",
